# Machine-readable runtime / tool versions for local development.
#
# Read by:
#   * asdf  -- https://asdf-vm.com/
#   * mise  -- https://mise.jdx.dev/    (drop-in successor to asdf-vm)
#   * rtx   -- archived; mise replaces it
#
# Single source of truth for "what versions does this repo expect on a
# dev machine". CI uses its own pins (.github/workflows/ci.yml), but
# they MUST match this file; if they drift, lint findings on a dev
# machine differ from CI findings, which is exactly the bug this file
# closes (Track H.1, v1.0.7).
#
# Update protocol:
#   1. Bump the version here.
#   2. Bump the corresponding pin in .github/workflows/ci.yml (and
#      .golangci.yml `run.go:` directive if Go itself moved).
#   3. Run `tools/install-lint.sh` (or `asdf install` / `mise install`)
#      and confirm `golangci-lint version` matches.
#   4. Run `golangci-lint run --timeout=5m ./...` and fix any new
#      findings the new version surfaces before merging.

# Go 1.26.x: the toolchain CI uses for build / test / lint. The
# go.mod `go 1.23.0` directive is the consumer floor (separate
# concept) — bumping the toolchain does not bump consumers' minimum
# required Go version.
golang 1.26.6

# golangci-lint 2.12.2: matches the v2-binary pin in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml::lint::golangci/golangci-lint-action@v8.0.0.
# Older v1 binaries (≤ 1.64.x) cannot read the v2 schema in
# .golangci.yml at all; they error out on `linters.default: none`.
# Newer v2 binaries are fine but might surface findings the CI pin
# does not — keep the version exact.
golangci-lint 2.12.2
